# ⚙️ Budget Management API (Backend)

![Java](https://img.shields.io/badge/Java-ED8B00?style=for-the-badge&logo=openjdk&logoColor=white)
![Spring Boot](https://img.shields.io/badge/Spring_Boot-6DB33F?style=for-the-badge&logo=spring-boot&logoColor=white)
![Hibernate](https://img.shields.io/badge/Hibernate-59666C?style=for-the-badge&logo=Hibernate&logoColor=white)
![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker-2496ED?style=for-the-badge&logo=docker&logoColor=white)

This repository contains the **RESTful API backend** for my full-stack Budget Management application. It is engineered to handle all business logic, secure data persistence, and client-server communication for the frontend dashboard.

Developed during my professional software development internship at CV Corp, this backend is built on a strict layered architecture and is fully containerized for cloud deployment.

**🔗 [View Frontend Repository](https://github.com/Yaswanth0690/budget-management-frontend)** | **🔗 [View Live App](https://yaswanth-budget-management.vercel.app/)**

## ✨ Key Features
* **RESTful Architecture:** Exposes clean, well-documented API endpoints for expense tracking, budget allocation, and user management.
* **Layered Design:** Strictly separates concerns across Controllers, Services, and Repositories for scalable and maintainable code.
* **ORM Integration:** Utilizes Spring Data JPA and Hibernate for seamless database interactions and dialect management.
* **Cloud & Container Ready:** Includes a configured `Dockerfile` and CORS policy handling for deployment to cloud environments (e.g., Oracle Cloud).

## 🛠️ Tech Stack
* **Language:** Java
* **Framework:** Spring Boot
* **Data Access:** Spring Data JPA / Hibernate
* **Build Tool:** Maven
* **Containerization:** Docker

